WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:05.480
Right off the bat, it's important to note
that History Channel currently has no public

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:10.730
plans to replace Frank Fritz, the longtime
co-host of the hit reality series "American

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:11.730
Pickers."

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.570
Representatives from the network said as much
in a recent statement to Us Weekly.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:21.070
That said, the departure of Fritz, confirmed
by the History Channel in late July of 2021,

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:25.650
will leave a substantial hole in the program
when it returns for its 23rd season.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.410
"American Pickers" has benefited from its
stars' unique interpersonal dynamic for more

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:35.180
than a decade, and it's hard to imagine anyone
stepping up to the plate that could match

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.410
Fritz's contributions to the show.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.660
It's equally hard to imagine, however, that
the production team won't be making some phone

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.550
calls in the near future, hoping to find a
new on-screen partner for Mike Wolfe.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:51.560
Fans have already started speculating about
who might take over for Fritz — so has Fritz,

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.730
in point of fact, who went so far as to voice
his opinions publicly.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.890
The recently ousted Picker told the Sun in
a recent interview,

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.440
"I think Mike wants to get his brother Robbie
in there to replace me.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.310
I don't know why he's behaving like that towards
me.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:09.100
You couldn't just stick two people in a van
and get the chemistry you get from me and

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.100
Mike."

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.100
Harsh?

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.670
Certainly, but that doesn't mean that History
won't tempt fate by seeing if they can catch

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.830
lightning in an antique bottle a second time.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:22.890
Frank Fritz isn't alone in his belief that
Robbie Wolfe might be "Pickering" up where

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:23.950
he left off.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:28.590
The second Wolfe brother has made more than
a few appearances on "American Pickers" already,

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.230
garnering a substantial social media following
along the way.

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:37.060
He's leveraged his popularity on the show
to establish himself as a successful antiquer

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.659
in his own right, running his shop and website
for buying and selling vintage goods.

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:46.370
There's no shame in keeping it in the family,
and the self-described "historian and lifelong

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:51.070
picker of antiques" would be a natural fit
for the show moving forward, should the people

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:53.690
in charge decide that a new co-host is in
order.

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.070
"Nice to see you.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:56.070
Robbie."

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.070
"Robbie.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:58.090
You talk to Danielle on the phone?'

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:02.620
Of course, Robbie isn't the only "American
Pickers" alum with skin in the game.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:06.420
History has already confirmed that Danielle
Colby, who has been with the show since its

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:12.370
debut episode in 2010, will continue to work
on the series during its upcoming season.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:16.350
The potential for Colby to get out from behind
the counter more often seems very much in

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.350
play.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:21.290
Bringing her one-of-a-kind perspective to
"American Pickers" on a regular basis could

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:26.410
mark a dramatic change of pace for the show
— her website bio describes her as a person

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:31.060
constantly, quote, "searching for answers
and back stories that will help nurture the

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:36.620
human spirit and at times allow us to sit
in quiet reflection with the more macabre

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.180
side of history."

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:42.940
Additionally, playing a larger role on the
series could potentially afford Colby a platform

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:46.530
for bringing attention to causes that she
feels passionate about.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:51.190
According to her social media, Colby has been
in Puerto Rico recently, dedicating her time

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:56.810
to orphanages, animal shelters, and raising
awareness about the human trafficking crisis.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:02.870
Meanwhile, "Jersey" Jon Szalay, Frank's interim
replacement from the season 22 premiere "Pumps,

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:08.070
Prints, and Picks," earned himself a few new
fans thanks to his motorcycle expertise and

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:13.060
obvious enthusiasm for the work over the course
of a few guest appearances this year.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:18.340
He's described Mike Wolfe as his "soul brother"
on social media following their on-camera

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:23.520
cross-country adventures, and his expertise
in the field of car and motorcycle restoration

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.530
would be a welcome addition to the program.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:30.450
Then again, and we're just throwing this out
there, Mike Wolfe did make a cameo appearance

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:35.550
on "NCIS" a couple of seasons back, lending
his expertise to Gibbs when a murder involving

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.840
an antique bludgeon had the constabulary flummoxed.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:42.739
"Please tell me that you didn't kill somebody."

00:03:42.739 --> 00:03:48.150
Mark Harmon hasn't been shy about discussing
his intention to leave the hit CBS series

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:52.140
since around the time that it was old enough
to get a driver's license, and there are worse

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.420
retirement plans than travelling the country
looking at cool stuff for money.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:01.400
Most importantly, the man behind Jethro Gibbs
would have a lot to contribute to the "American

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:06.069
Pickers" family — for example, if the team
ever needed to move a boat out of a basement,

00:04:06.069 --> 00:04:08.370
Harmon would basically be the guy to call.

